These experiments utilize a variant of gated recurrent unit which is defined as follows:

\displaystyle\begin{pmatrix}{\bf z}_{t}\\ {\bf r}_{t}\end{pmatrix} \displaystyle= \displaystyle{\bf W}_{h}{\bf h}_{t-1}+{\bf W}_{x}{\bf x}_{t} \displaystyle\hat{{\bf h}}_{t} \displaystyle= \displaystyle\text{tanh}({\bf W}{\bf x}_{t}+\sigma({\bf r}_{t})\odot({\bf U}{\bf h}_{t-1})) \displaystyle{\bf h}_{t} \displaystyle= \displaystyle(1-\sigma({\bf z}_{t})){\bf h}_{t-1}+\sigma({\bf z}_{t})\hat{{\bf h}}_{t}

Layer normalization is applied as follows:

\displaystyle\begin{pmatrix}{\bf z}_{t}\\ {\bf r}_{t}\end{pmatrix} \displaystyle= \displaystyle LN({\bf W}_{h}{\bf h}_{t-1};\bm{\alpha}_{1},\bm{\beta}_{1})+LN({\bf W}_{x}{\bf x}_{t};\bm{\alpha}_{2},\bm{\beta}_{2}) \displaystyle\hat{{\bf h}}_{t} \displaystyle= \displaystyle\text{tanh}(LN({\bf W}{\bf x}_{t};\bm{\alpha}_{3},\bm{\beta}_{3})+\sigma({\bf r}_{t})\odot LN({\bf U}{\bf h}_{t-1};\bm{\alpha}_{4},\bm{\beta}_{4})) \displaystyle{\bf h}_{t} \displaystyle= \displaystyle(1-\sigma({\bf z}_{t})){\bf h}_{t-1}+\sigma({\bf z}_{t})\hat{{\bf h}}_{t}

just as before, $\bm{\alpha}_{i}$ is initialized to a vector of zeros and each $\bm{\beta}_{i}$ is initialized to a vector of ones.
